# Nougat extraction stub — s100-017 (Jonak et al. 2016)

**Status:** NOT RUN. Nougat re-extraction was not required for this paper.

## Rationale

The primary paper (Jonak et al. 2016, BMC Systems Biology 10:75) and all 10
BMC open-access supplementary files (MOESM1..10) are **born-digital PDFs with
a text layer** — not scanned images. The extraction step used
`pdftotext -layout` and produced clean, complete text for:

- Paper body (`ocr/raw_layout.txt`)
- MOESM1 (equations 1–72 — the ODE system) → `ocr/MOESM1.txt`
- MOESM2 (Haseltine–Rawlings hybrid algorithm) → `ocr/MOESM2.txt`
- MOESM3 (initial-condition tables) → `ocr/MOESM3.txt`
- MOESM4 (parameter tables 1–5, ~110 rate constants) → `ocr/MOESM4.txt`
- MOESM5, MOESM6 (Kracikova cell-fate description) → `ocr/MOESM5..6.txt`

Line-by-line diff against the parameter transcription in
`code/parameters.py` found 3 discrepancies, all traced to non-breaking-space
codepoints mid-number in the PDF (a known pdftotext artefact); manually fixed.

## Why Nougat was not needed

Nougat is preferred over pdftotext for:
- Scanned/image-only PDFs (this paper is text-layer)
- Complex mathematical notation that pdftotext mangles (this paper's LaTeX-
  compiled equations survive pdftotext -layout cleanly, verified against the
  BMC HTML version)
- Papers with heavy multi-column layout (this paper is single-column)

None of those conditions applied. Running Nougat would consume GPU time for
no informational gain.

## If Nougat re-extraction is later required

Command template:
```
nougat source/paper.pdf --out extraction/nougat_output/ --recompute
```
Would produce `extraction/nougat_output/paper.mmd`. On UICGPU A100:
~2–3 min per PDF; ~30 min for all 11 files (paper + 10 supps).

Free-endpoint compliant (UICGPU is idle-A100, part of Rick's standing
small-batch OCR compute allocation).

